## Why This Is Asked
Tests crossing-boundary bit extraction on a 128-bit value with no branching, mirroring real-world crypto/low-level data parsing tasks.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-boundary bit manipulation.
- Mask generation for widths up to 64 without 64-bit overflow.
- Handling 128-bit values via hi/lo halves (no loops).

## Code Example
```javascript
function extractBits128(hi, lo, pos, width) {
  const V = (BigInt(hi) << 64n) | BigInt(lo);
  const mask = width === 64 ? (1n << 64n) - 1n : (1n << BigInt(width)) - 1n;
  return (V >> BigInt(pos)) & mask;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason about cross-boundary bit interactions and implement constant-time checks using only bitwise ops. 

## Key Concepts
- Bitwise shifts and masks across multiword values
- Detecting adjacent bits within each 64-bit half and across the 64-bit boundary
- Branchless boolean results for interview clarity

## Code Example
```javascript
int hasAdjacentOnes128(uint128 x) {
  uint64_t a = x.lo & (x.lo << 1);
  uint64_t b = x.hi & (x.hi << 1);
  int cross = ((x.lo >> 63) & 1) & (x.hi & 1);
  return (a | b | cross) != 0;
}
```

