## Why This Is Asked
Branchless 128-bit comparison is common in crypto/hash pipelines and requires careful borrow logic across halves. It tests low-level reasoning without relying on 128-bit native ops.

## Key Concepts
- 128-bit numbers split into hi/lo.
- Borrow propagation across 64-bit halves.
- Branchless evaluation using comparisons on unsigned integers.

## Code Example
```c
uint8_t lessThan128(uint128 a, uint128 b){
  uint64_t loDiff = a.lo - b.lo;
  uint64_t borrowLo = (a.lo < b.lo);
  uint64_t hiDiff = a.hi - b.hi - borrowLo;
  uint64_t borrowHi = (a.hi < b.hi + borrowLo);
  return (uint8_t)borrowHi;
}
```

